# AWS domains — Console, regional API endpoints, static assets
# Resolved IPs end up in ipset vpn_domains via /etc/dnsmasq.d/vpn-domains-aws.conf
# Generated dnsmasq directives match the listed domain AND all its subdomains,
# so wildcard parents cover most cases (e.g. amazonaws.com → s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com).

# --- Global (covers all regions and most services) ---
# All *.amazonaws.com regional/service endpoints: s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com,
# ec2.us-west-2.amazonaws.com, dynamodb.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com, etc.
amazonaws.com

# AWS Console UI, signin, docs, marketing.
aws.amazon.com

# Static console assets (CDN-fronted): a0.awsstatic.com etc.
awsstatic.com
a.b.cdn.console.awsstatic.com

# Console CDN edge with random subdomains: a.b.cdn.console.awstatic.com,
# *.cdn.console.awstatic.com — note: separate domain from awsstatic.com,
# Amazon uses both. Verified via SOA: both delegate to awsdns-*.
awstatic.com

# Misc Amazon-controlled control-plane assets used by Console.
a2z.com
aws.dev

# --- us-east-1 (N. Virginia) — explicit hosts in case wildcard match misses ---
us-east-1.amazonaws.com
us-east-1.console.aws.amazon.com
us-east-1.signin.aws.amazon.com
oidc.us-east-1.amazonaws.com

# --- us-west-2 (Oregon) — explicit hosts ---
us-west-2.amazonaws.com
us-west-2.console.aws.amazon.com
us-west-2.signin.aws.amazon.com
oidc.us-west-2.amazonaws.com

# --- Notes ---
# - cloudfront.net is intentionally NOT listed: it would route every
#   CloudFront customer (millions of sites) through the VPN. Add specific
#   distribution IDs (e.g. d2c5q2y2zvrvg6.cloudfront.net) only if the
#   Console or a service really needs them and you've confirmed the host
#   in the browser network tab.
# - amazonaws.com.cn (AWS China) and amazonaws-us-gov.com (GovCloud) are
#   intentionally NOT listed — different infrastructure, add only on demand.

continuum.console.api.aws
